ENG-17  A game's request for a display mode is answered without switching the Mac's display.
Component: lby-trixie-fullscreen (native full screen and the screen's size), patches/lby-trixie-fullscreen/.

dlls/winemac.drv/display.c (winemac.so). Written 2026-11-15, LGPL-2.1-or-later like Wine.

What: Modern Warfare Remastered (D3D11, DXMT) asks Wine for 3024x1964 at 47 Hz ("Setting display mode" in the log). macdrv_ChangeDisplaySettings found the Mac's low-resolution
3024x1964 mode (1x, 48 Hz, no Retina) and switched the whole screen to it: the desktop shrank into the upper left corner, windows came out in a mess, the Dock and menu bar were drawn
for the old size, and the mode came back only when the game was closed (measured 2026-11-15: 1512x982 points, 3024x1964 pixels, 120 Hz -> 3024x1964 points, 48 Hz -> back). Native full screen was
switched off by a launch option and it happened all the same, so it is the engine's own display-mode switch. Now the call answers "done" and the display keeps its mode; native full screen (ENG-12, ENG-15) scales a window that is smaller than the screen. One line `lullaby:displaymode kept ...` in the wine log, once a run.
Requires: nothing. A game that really needs the Mac switched (an old game wanting 640x480 for itself) gets the answer but not the switch: its window is scaled by ENG-15 in native full screen.
Other bases: Dormison's display.c is the unchanged Wine one in this place.
Test: Modern Warfare Remastered (DXMT): the desktop stays at 1512x982 points while the game runs (read with a display watcher: CGDisplayCopyDisplayMode every second), the game's picture is not stretched; RE9, PEAK, Isaac, ETS 2 unchanged (none of them asks for a mode).
Verified on: not yet.
Switch: LULLABY_KEEP_DISPLAY_MODE=0 as a launch option gives the old behaviour for a run; on by default (the old behaviour changes the whole Mac's resolution).

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/display.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/display.c
